{
  "analysis": "The reviewer describes the genie game feature: a wheel spins, stops on a high prize, and then the genie moves the wheel so the outcome becomes a spin tag with a much lower prize. This is a claim that the game overrides or manipulates the displayed outcome of the wheel, concealing how results are actually determined — the wheel's stop is not what it appears. The wheel itself is also a chance-based reward delivery system with variable outcomes. No real-money stake is mentioned, so Gambling does not apply.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "P_IllusionOfControl",
      "span": "whe the wheel spin after stopping on a great price the genie move the wheel to a spin tag, and then the prices after the spin are way lower than the original price, from 100 million with 5x multiplier to a 48 million",
      "rule_applied": "definition / vs Alleged rigging boundary rule",
      "rationale": "The span asserts the game manipulates the wheel's outcome after it stops, downgrading the displayed prize — the game conceals how outcomes are determined, deceiving the player about the result."
    },
    {
      "label": "P_RewardMania",
      "span": "whe the wheel spin after stopping on a great price the genie move the wheel to a spin tag",
      "rule_applied": "Variable Rewards [low-level]",
      "rationale": "The spin wheel is a chance-based, unpredictable reward delivery mechanism; under the vs Alleged rigging rule, the rigging claim does not nullify Reward Mania, so both apply under R9."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The reviewer complains about three things. First, a 30-second wait to connect to a match: this is matchmaking/queue time arising from the operation of the service, not an in-game timer gating play, so it does not meet Wait to Play. Second, rewards that look generous but are 'just for show': no mechanism of delivery is described, so this is an evaluation of reward value, not Reward Mania. Third, weapon upgrades and perks are difficult to get and the player is 'stick battling to win': the reviewer describes having to keep battling repeatedly as the route to progress, which names the repeated activity (battling) tied to advancement, satisfying Grinding. 'Rob you of your time' is a general evaluation and codes nothing on its own.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_Grinding",
      "span": "Its difficult to get weapon upgrades or any percs others you stick battling to win",
      "rule_applied": "definition; boundary rule vs Slow Progress",
      "rationale": "The span names the repeated activity (battling to win) as what the player must keep doing to obtain upgrades, i.e., repetitive play as the means of progress."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The reviewer describes Clash Royale's trophy ladder: after 8k trophies they repeatedly face the same powerful cards (mega knight, pekka, golem), which is play against other players, so Competition applies. They also state the game is 'pay to win' and that skill alone won't move you higher, which is the Pay to Win low-level pattern under Pay to Progress. The complaints about cards needing rebuffing and being spammed are balance grievances; nothing says a purchased item lost value after acquisition, so Power Creep does not lift. 'You have to go out of your way to be annoying to actually win' describes player conduct, not a game incentive rewarding dishonest or harmful play, so Encourages Anti-Social Behavior does not apply.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "all you play against after 8k trophies is mega knight,pekka, and golem",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The reviewer describes facing other players' decks on a trophy ladder, i.e., the game pits players against each other."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_PayToProgress",
      "span": "its also pay to win and usually doesn't let you get higher from just using skill",
      "rule_applied": "Pay to Win [low-level]",
      "rationale": "States directly that spending grants advantage and that advancement is not achievable through skill alone."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The reviewer describes several mechanics. First, 'diamonds' are named as a premium-style in-game currency, but the span concerns customer service failing to compensate diamonds lost to a game element not appearing — a bug complaint, and no real-money conversion is described, so Intermediate Currency does not apply. Second, 'you don't have to pay to win' explicitly invokes pay-to-win: the reviewer frames paying as the route to winning while noting it is not mandatory, which establishes a paid advantage contrast. Third, 'don't buy from this game beyond the pass' names a purchasable pass, which under R5 is a battle pass / recurring fee instance. Fourth, 'Get friends and a team and trade lives' describes an existing resource-exchange mechanism between players already in the game, which is Reciprocity (not Forced Fellowship, since no recruitment of new players is described). The customer service complaint about the missing game element is attributed to a malfunction and codes nothing under R11.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_PayToProgress",
      "span": "It is a fun game, you don't have to pay to win.",
      "rule_applied": "Pay to Win [low-level]; Free alternative boundary rule",
      "rationale": "The phrase 'pay to win' explicitly describes spending money as a route to winning; the free/paid contrast establishes the paid advantage exists even though the reviewer says it is optional."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_RecurringFee",
      "span": "I suggest after this cust. svc experience that you don't buy from this game beyond the pass.",
      "rule_applied": "Battle passes [indicators]",
      "rationale": "The game contains a purchasable pass, which is an explicit instance of a recurring fee under R5."
    },
    {
      "label": "S_Reciprocity",
      "span": "Get friends and a team and trade lives.",
      "rule_applied": "definition; vs Reciprocity boundary under Forced Fellowship",
      "rationale": "Players already in the game exchange lives with teammates, a resource-transfer favour mechanism between existing players."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
